WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.020
Pulling up to another day of Tesla's short time, episode 532, it's July 5th, 2026, and

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:08.220
I'm Patrick in Vancouver.

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:10.680
Here's what's happening with Tesla today.

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:18.540
Strict lease terms left one driver facing $2,141 in wear and tear charges after returning

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:19.120
her Tesla.

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:26.040
Tesla reported a 25% year-over-year increase in global vehicle sales for the second quarter.

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:31.440
The figure represents the strongest quarterly sales total the company has posted to date.

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:37.680
Growth spanned all models even as US registrations showed softness during the same period.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:41.280
Shares fell sharply on the same day the results appeared.

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:47.320
The sales gain came one day after Rivian raised its own production outlook for 2026.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:52.840
Rivian increased its production and delivery guidance for the remainder of 2026.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:57.540
The adjustment came on the same day Tesla shares declined sharply.

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:02.880
The report contrasts the two companies near-term volume trajectories without providing

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:04.900
specific Rivian unit targets.

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:09.040
The guidance revision applied to the full second half of the year.

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:13.240
No commentary on competitive positioning accompanied the update.

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:18.400
The change coincided exactly with the release of Tesla's quarterly sales data.

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:24.180
While volume numbers improved, one model continues to dominate the broader EV market.

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:30.320
The model Y held the top position globally for May by a clear margin over competing battery

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:36.420
electric vehicles. The ranking reinforces Tesla's current product strength even as older vehicles

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:42.960
receive updates. No unit volumes were disclosed in the data. The result stands on the ranking alone.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:48.720
Strong sales rest partly on software that keeps both new and older cars competitive.

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:55.460
An over-the-air update reached millions of pre-HW-4 vehicles after repeated owner requests.

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:59.260
Recipients noted improvements in the delivered features.

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:04.500
Performance gaps versus HW-4 models remained visible to those drivers.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:08.920
Continued hardware differences stay a point of discussion among owners.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:14.420
Software's ability to manage vehicle physics also shows up in everyday driving conditions.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:20.620
Vehicle mass is a fixed physical property that software must accommodate rather than override.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:26.360
On low grip surfaces, the added weight increases both the force needed to change direction

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:32.080
and the time before traction is lost. Tesla's approach integrates motor torque response,

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:36.260
sensor fusion, and stability algorithms into one closed loop.

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:40.620
The system treats the entire powertrain as a single actuator.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:46.300
This produces faster recovery than traditional stability systems that cut power after slip is

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:51.880
detected. The same control layer supports future autonomy and ride quality claims.

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:58.000
While the engineering works in controlled demos, real-world customer experiences can still produce

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:05.800
friction. A returning less C received a $2,141 invoice for interior and exterior items.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:10.480
The charges covered wear that exceeded Tesla's inspection thresholds.

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:15.420
The customer described the standards as stricter than those of prior leases she had used.

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:20.540
Contract terms allow recovery of costs for any damage beyond normal use.

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:25.840
Short spot segment highlights how contract terms affect total cost at turn-in.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:29.180
Customer service friction appears in other areas as well.

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:35.440
A buyer attempting to secure a Tesla rebate encountered an issue when a staff member intervened

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:41.060
during the process. The customer stated she would never purchase from Tesla again following the

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:46.740
interaction. The report centers on the breakdown in the rebate handling rather than the vehicle's

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:52.160
specifications. The intervention occurred at the point of finalizing the rebate paperwork.

00:03:52.820 --> 00:03:56.860
No details on the specific rebate program were included in the account.

00:03:57.320 --> 00:04:01.080
The outcome led the buyer to declare an end to future Tesla purchases.

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:07.940
Google Maps added real-time occupancy data for superchargers visible to drivers of other electric

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:13.320
vehicles. The feature shows whether stalls are expected to be occupied upon arrival.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:18.760
It applies only to the portion of the network already opened to non-Tesla vehicles.

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:25.280
The addition represents continued expansion of Tesla's charging infrastructure beyond its own fleet.

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:30.760
Infrastructure reach also surfaces in product teases outside the car itself.

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:37.520
A marketing video for Tesla's new outdoor product line briefly showed an unreleased wireless speaker.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:44.420
The device appeared alongside camping and lifestyle items. No pricing or launch details were released.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:49.480
