00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:55.620
A production-intense cybercab appeared in public wearing a large patriotic vinyl wrap marking

00:04:55.620 --> 00:05:03.040
the US 250th anniversary. The wrap covered the vehicle's angular bodywork and drew immediate attention.

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:09.020
Observers noted the vehicle matched earlier prototype dimensions without visible sensor changes.

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:15.600
An owner examined a high mileage rental Model 3 after more than 204,000 miles of use.

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:21.860
The battery health reading and range retention exceeded typical expectations for that mileage level.

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:26.860
The inspection focused on degradation metrics rather than cosmetic condition.

00:05:27.620 --> 00:05:36.440
A GMC Sierra EV driver reported paying $93.85 for a single fast charge session on the EV Go network.

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:43.660
The owner calculated roughly $500 in annual savings if using Tesla's supercharging rates instead.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:48.660
The comparison centered on pricing per kilowatt hour rather than charging speed.

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:56.540
There is a challenge worth discussing. A returning LSE received an unexpected $2,141 bill for

00:05:56.540 --> 00:06:02.100
wear that exceeded Tesla's thresholds. The customer described the inspection standards as

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:08.140
stricter than those of other lessores. This creates a point of friction at turn-in for some customers.

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:13.420
Tesla stated that its vehicles rank as the most American-made cars available.

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:20.600
The post tied the claim directly to the country's 250th anniversary. No additional production or

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:26.840
